###Question: Diurnal variations in blood pressure are influenced by:
###Options:
A.  a.	A consistent intake of high-sodium diet;
B.  b.	Circadian rhythms regulated by the hypothalamic-pituitary-adrenal axis;
C.  c.	The phase of the moon and its effect on tides;
D.  d.	The use of tricyclic antidepressants during nighttime.

###Answer: B.  b.  Circadian rhythms regulated by the hypothalamic-pituitary-adrenal axis;
###Explanation: Diurnal variations in blood pressure are significantly influenced by the body’s circadian rhythms, which are, in turn, regulated by the hypothalamic-pituitary-adrenal (HPA) axis. The HPA axis plays a critical role in the stress response, affecting various physiological processes, including the secretion of hormones such as cortisol,

